Package: emeraldian
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: terminal UI for an Obsidian vault
 emeraldian browses a directory of Markdown notes the way Obsidian does. It
 lists the vault, live-previews a note, resolves [[wikilinks]] into backlinks
 and an outline, renders images inline where the terminal supports it, and
 draws the link structure as a force-directed graph.
 .
 The assistant panel talks to an LLM over the network and is inert until
 configured with an endpoint and a key; nothing else here needs a network.
 .
 Its HTTP client carries a compiled-in copy of the Mozilla root store rather
 than reading /etc/ssl/certs, so the assistant's TLS trust does not follow the
 system and a distrusted root needs a new build to take effect. That is also
 why this package does not depend on ca-certificates.
